{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGaXqFCtxUh83stj9QhV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```python\nimport re\n\ndef slugify(title):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", title.lower()).strip(\"-\")\n\ndef unique_slug(title, existing):\n    base = slugify(title)\n    slug = base\n    n = 2\n    while slug in existing:\n        slug = f\"{base}-{n}\"\n        n += 1\n    return slug\n```\n\nFor example, `unique_slug(\"Hello World\", {\"hello-world\", \"hello-world-2\"})` returns `\"hello-world-3\"`.\n\n- **No mutation:** The function doesn't add the result to `existing`. The caller does that if they want the slug reserved.\n- **Empty slugs:** A title with no alphanumerics, like `\"!!!\"`, slugifies to `\"\"`. That gives `\"\"`, then `\"-2\"`, `\"-3\"`, and so on. If that can happen in your data, add a fallback such as `base = slugify(title) or \"untitled\"`.\n\nI didn't see a file path, so I haven't edited anything. Tell me which file it belongs in and I'll add it there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3542,"cache_read_input_tokens":16450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3542,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c7325fc-30f1-47fc-bf29-1f165c8ef96e","uuid":"b66ecd7c-dc9f-4c90-be89-2e54c8dc50dd","timestamp":"2026-11-21T18:53:03.178Z","request_id":"req_011ChGaXpwquqKE39eGSQN5A"}
